Package: MDFA
Type: Package
Title: Matrix Decomposition Factor Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yoshikazu", "Terada", email = "terada.yoshikazu.es@osaka-u.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Description: Matrix Decomposition Factor Analysis (MDFA) was proposed as a
    matrix factorization-based approach to factor analysis, but its
    statistical properties had remained largely unexplored for many years.
    Terada (2025) <arXiv:2403.06968> showed that MDFA is a minimum
    discrepancy function estimator based on the Bures-Wasserstein distance,
    thereby establishing its consistency and asymptotic normality. This
    package performs exploratory factor analysis using MDFA via an
    alternating least squares algorithm (see Adachi and Trendafilov (2018)
    <doi:10.1007/s11336-017-9600-y> for algorithm details) or a
    quasi-Newton (BFGS) algorithm. Standard errors and confidence intervals
    for the loadings are estimated from nonparametric bootstrap
    replications of the estimation procedure.
